from flask import Flask, render_template, request
from flask_sqlalchemy import SQLAlchemy
from datetime import datetime 

Imports: Imports necessary modules and classes to create a Flask web application, SQLAlchemy for database integration, and datetime for timestamps.



app = Flask(__name__)
app.config['SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI'] = 'sqlite:///db.db'
app.config['SQLALCHEMY_TRACK_MODIFICATIONS'] = False
db = SQLAlchemy(app)

App Initialization and Configuration: Creates a Flask application, configures SQLAlchemy to use a SQLite database, and disables unnecessary modification tracking.



class Message(db.Model):
    id = db.Column(db.Integer, primary_key=True)
    user = db.Column(db.String(200), nullable=True)
    content = db.Column(db.String(500), nullable=True)
    created_at = db.Column(db.DateTime(), default=datetime.now)

Database Model: Defines a Message model with fields id, user, content, and created_at for storing messages in the database.
